# nomi golden outputs — do not hand-edit
#
# The VM's output is checked against this file: a written-down answer,
# not another engine's.
# See internal/expectation/expectation.go for what is masked and why.
# Regenerate with NOMI_REGENERATE_EXPECTATIONS=1 and name the reason for
# every moved record in the commit message.
#
# C <id> / E <exit> / N <declared cases> / H <sha256 of transcript>
# S <source line>, only for a record that carries its own program
# T <transcript line>, verbatim
population irbuild
what one record per program an internal/irbuild test compares the VM against, keyed <entry>@<sha256(its files, .nomi files as tokens)[:16]>, run as the command that owns it would run it. <dir> is the program's directory. A temp program carries its files as source; a repository program's entry is its path from the worktree root.
